      "name": "SetConfigValue",
      "signature": "BOOL SetConfigValue(int nConfigId, dword dwValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "Validates and sets a configuration value for a specific config ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Compare nConfigId against 0xB (11 decimal)\n  2. If nConfigId != 0xB, return FALSE (invalid ID)\n  3. If nConfigId == 0xB, store dwValue in global g_dwConfigValue\n  4. Return TRUE (success)\n\nParameters:\n  ECX: nConfigId - Configuration ID to validate (only 0xB is accepted)\n  EDX: dwValue - Configuration value to store in global storage\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 1 (TRUE): Configuration accepted and stored successfully\n  EAX = 0 (FALSE): Invalid configuration ID (not equal to 0xB)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Rejects all config IDs except 0xB\n  - Always overwrites global storage regardless of previous value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5c22dede0f74ae8b02dbfc7aae0ebe58",
