      "name": "GetVideoPlayerContext",
      "signature": "void * GetVideoPlayerContext(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Returns pointer to video player context structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global video player state pointer from g_pVideoPlayerState\n2. Dereference at offset 0x14 to retrieve context pointer\n3. Return the context pointer in EAX\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nEAX = void pointer to video player context structure (or NULL if not initialized)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- May return NULL if video player not yet initialized\n- Context pointer is obtained from offset 0x14 in the state structure\n- Function is a simple accessor/thunk with no error handling\n\nStructure Layout (g_pVideoPlayerState):\nOffset  Size  Field              Type         Description\n0x00    4     [padding]          -            -\n0x04    4     [padding]          -            -\n0x08    4     [padding]          -            -\n0x0C    4     [padding]          -            -\n0x10    4     [padding]          -            -\n0x14    4     pContext           void*        Video player context pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x14 = Offset to context pointer within video player state structure\n\nError Handling:\nNone - Direct dereference with no validation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5df2c7f1ec461c378315e6d72308a5a7",
