      "name": "NormalizeRectangleCoordinates",
      "signature": "void NormalizeRectangleCoordinates(int * prcBounds, byte byProcessCorners)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Normalizes rectangle coordinates: ensures left < right and top < bottom.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract right (high 32-bits) and left (low 32-bits) from 64-bit prcBounds[0:1]\n2. Validate left < right; normalize via FUN_6f8e4f5f if invalid (assertion at D2DDr:0x149)\n3. Extract top from prcBounds[1] and bottom from prcBounds[3]\n4. Validate top < bottom; normalize via FUN_6f8e4f5f if invalid (assertion at D2DDr:0x14a)\n5. If normalized coords differ AND top != bottom: call FUN_6f8e3a40 four times for corner processing\n\nParameters:\n- prcBounds (ECX): int* pointing to [left, top, right, bottom] rectangle structure\n- byProcessCorners: byte flag controlling corner processing via FUN_6f8e3a40\n\nReturns:\nvoid; modifies rectangle coordinates in-place through prcBounds and FUN_6f8e4f5f side effects\n\nPhantom Variables:\n- uVar1: Assembly-only temporary (CONCAT44 result combining left/right). Ghidra decompiler phantom.\n\nNotes:\nAppears to normalize invalid rectangles for rendering or collision detection. Assertion failures indicate invalid input bounds in debug builds. Used by display/rendering subsystem.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:546c17e22a38a8e15c8829671ea3e893",
