      "name": "CloseSmackVideoPlayer",
      "signature": "void CloseSmackVideoPlayer(int * pVideoContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes and cleans up Smack video player resources.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Check if global Smack pool allocation exists (g_dwSmackPoolAllocation != 0)\n    2. If pool exists, call ReleasePoolAllocation to free pool memory\n    3. Set g_dwSmackPoolAllocation to 0 to mark as released\n    4. Check video context type tag at offset +4 for 's' (0x73 = Smack format)\n    5. If Smack type and handle at offset +0 is non-NULL:\n       a. Call SmackClose to close the Smack video handle\n       b. Set handle at offset +0 to NULL\n\n  Parameters:\n    pVideoContext (ECX) - Pointer to video context structure:\n      +0x00: Smack handle (pointer to Smack structure)\n      +0x04: Type tag byte ('s' = Smack, 'b' = Bink)\n\n  Returns:\n    void - No return value\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Pool release is unconditional if g_dwSmackPoolAllocation is set\n    - Smack close only occurs if type tag is 's' AND handle is non-NULL\n    - Safe to call with NULL handle (checked before SmackClose)\n\n  Structure Layout (VideoContext at pVideoContext):\n    Offset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n    0x00    4     hSmack      void*   Handle to Smack video structure\n    0x04    1     byType      char    Video format type tag ('s'=Smack, 'b'=Bink)\n\n  Magic Numbers:\n    0x73 (115) - ASCII 's' indicating Smack video format\n    0xF0 (240) - Pool allocation size passed to ReleasePoolAllocation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:264a3f73902bf2dfa7abce5079176c7b",
