      "name": "InitializeSubsystem",
      "signature": "void InitializeSubsystem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes subsystem through sequential function calls and stores configuration data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call first initialization function (FUN_1001cfc0) to prepare subsystem\n2. Call configuration function (FUN_1001de35) and store return value in global DAT_1003c8ac\n3. Call finalization function (FUN_1001dde5) with implicit context from step 2\n4. Clear FPU status flags with FNCLEX instruction\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe function uses implicit register passing where FUN_1001de35 returns a value in EAX (stored in DAT_1003c8ac) and also sets ECX register which is implicitly passed to FUN_1001dde5. The FNCLEX instruction clears floating-point unit status, suggesting this initialization may involve mathematical computations.\n\nIMPLICIT: ECX register set by FUN_1001de35 and passed to FUN_1001dde5",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
