      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Configures subsystem initialization parameters with predefined buffer and flag values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_1001fc6c with context pointer and two configuration constants\n2. Pass 0x10000 (65536) as buffer size parameter\n3. Pass 0x30000 (196608) as flags/configuration parameter\n4. Return immediately after configuration call\n\nParameters:\npContext - Pointer to InitContext structure containing subsystem state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, configuration applied through context pointer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10000 (65536) - Buffer size parameter, likely initial buffer allocation\n0x30000 (196608) - Configuration flags parameter, specifies subsystem options",
