      "name": "ProcessLocaleStringTransform",
      "signature": "void ProcessLocaleStringTransform(LocaleContext * pLocaleContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes locale-specific string transformation with character skipping and rotation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert first character of input string to lowercase using ConvertCharacterToLowerCase\n2. If converted character equals 'e' (0x65), skip to character rotation step  \n3. Otherwise, enter character skipping loop\n4. Advance string pointer to next character\n5. Check locale mode via global DAT_1002e914 (< 2 = table lookup, >= 2 = function call)\n6. For table lookup mode: Use PTR_DAT_1002e708 lookup table with character * 2 offset, mask with 0x4\n7. For function call mode: Call FUN_1001fbc2 with character value and constant 4\n8. Continue until character test returns 0 (non-whitespace character found)\n9. Perform character rotation at end of string\n10. Save current character and replace with global DAT_1002e918\n11. Iterate through remaining string, shifting characters one position\n12. Continue until null terminator reached\n\nParameters:\npLocaleContext - Locale context object containing character mapping data and locale settings\nlpszString - Input string to process and transform in-place\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies string in-place, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf first character converts to 'e' (0x65), skips whitespace removal entirely\nString rotation uses global character value DAT_1002e918 as insertion point\nFunction handles two different locale modes based on DAT_1002e914 threshold\nCharacter lookup table uses stride of 2 bytes per character entry\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x65 - ASCII 'e', threshold for skipping whitespace removal\n0x4 - Bitmask for character classification in lookup table  \n0x2 - Stride multiplier for lookup table access (PTR_DAT_1002e708[char * 2])\nDAT_1002e914 - Locale mode selector (< 2 = table, >= 2 = function)\nDAT_1002e918 - Character value used for string rotation\nPTR_DAT_1002e708 - Character classification lookup table pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
