      "signature": "void * FUN_6fd23263(void * pValue, void * pBuffer, int nWidth, int nPrecision)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Converts a floating-point number to string representation with width/precision control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load 64-bit double value from param_1 into x87 FPU stack\n  2. Call FUN_6f8e7255 to decompose double into mantissa (64-bit, stored in local_14) \n     and exponent representation\n  3. Check mantissa for '-' sign marker (0x2d byte) to detect negative numbers\n  4. Calculate output buffer starting offset:\n     - Base offset from nWidth parameter (0 if nWidth <= 0, else 1)\n     - Additional offset if mantissa indicates negative number\n  5. Call FUN_6f8e71de to position buffer pointer based on calculated offset\n  6. Call FUN_6f8e55fc to apply decimal formatting using nPrecision specification\n  7. Return pointer to pBuffer containing formatted decimal string\n\nParameters:\n  pValue     - Pointer to double IEEE 754 value (64-bit) [EBP+0x8]\n  pBuffer    - Output character buffer for string result [EBP+0xc]\n  nWidth     - Field width specification (0=no padding, >0=right-align) [EBP+0x10]\n  nPrecision - Decimal digits specification [EBP+0x14]\n\nReturns:\n  pBuffer    - Pointer to formatted string result (null-terminated)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Negative numbers detected by checking mantissa for 0x2d ('-') marker\n  - Width <= 0 results in left-aligned output with single offset\n  - Width > 0 applies right-alignment padding calculations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
