      "signature": "char * FUN_6fd23386(double * pValue, char * szBuffer, SIZE_T nWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Converts a double-precision floating-point number to a string representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Loads the double value from the pointer parameter\n  2. Calls internal formatting function to extract mantissa and exponent (0x6f8e7255)\n  3. Handles sign conversion and negative number prefix ('-' or '+')\n  4. Calls function to format digits with proper decimal point placement (0x6f8e71de)\n  5. Appends formatted result to output buffer with bounds checking (0x6f8e5713)\n  6. Returns pointer to output buffer (or end of written string)\n\nParameters:\n  pValue (param_1, [EBP+0x8]): Pointer to double value to convert\n  pBuffer (param_2, [EBP+0xc]): Output buffer to receive formatted string\n  nWidth (param_3, [EBP+0x10]): Maximum width/size of output buffer\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: Pointer to output buffer containing the formatted string (or end of string)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles negative numbers by adding '-' prefix\n  - Uses internal flag structure (aFlags) to track formatting options\n  - Checks for sign condition at offset 0x2d to determine sign character\n  - Respects buffer size constraints during string building",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:bcdf5117db791c61e9ee045fb25e0af2",
