      "name": "DisplayRuntimeError",
      "signature": "void DisplayRuntimeError(uint dwErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Displays a runtime error message dialog or stderr output based on error code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Linear search g_aErrorCodeTable for entry matching dwErrorCode\n  2. Calculate table index from search result (offset into paired code/message table)\n  3. If match found, check exit mode:\n     - Mode 0x01 or (Mode 0x00 && g_fForceCleanup): Write message to stderr via WriteFile\n     - Otherwise: Continue to dialog display\n  4. Special case: If code is 0xfc, skip all message display and exit\n  5. Get module filename into szModulePath buffer (0x104 bytes)\n  6. If GetModuleFileNameA fails, use default string \"<program name unknown>\"\n  7. Truncate path to 0x3c (60) chars if needed, append \"...\" suffix\n  8. Build error message: \"Runtime Error!\n\nProgram: [path]\n[message]\n[details]\"\n  9. Display message box with title \"Microsoft Visual C++ Runtime Library\" (flags 0x12010)\n\nParameters:\n  dwErrorCode (uint, EBP+0x8): Runtime error code (0x02, 0x08, 0x09, 0xfc, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Does not return normally (exits or cleans up)",
