      "name": "ClearBitAndTruncateHigh",
      "signature": "int ClearBitAndTruncateHigh(int * pBitfield, int nBitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Clears a bit at the specified index and truncates all higher bits in a 96-bit bitfield.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate word index by dividing bit index by 0x20 (32)\n2. Calculate bit position within word using modulo 0x20\n3. Get pointer to the target 32-bit word in the bitfield\n4. Calculate bit shift value as (0x1F - bit_position)\n5. Check if the target bit is currently set using bit mask\n6. If bit is set and no higher bits are set (via CheckBitfieldSlotAvailable), call FUN_1001fde6 with previous index\n7. Clear the target bit using AND with inverted bit mask\n8. Calculate starting word for high-bit clearing (word_index + 1)\n9. If more words exist (word_index < 2), clear all remaining high words\n10. Return the value from step 6 or 0 if bit was not set\n\nParameters:\npBitfield - Pointer to 96-bit bitfield (3 x 32-bit words, 12 bytes total)\nnBitIndex - Zero-based bit position to clear (0-95 range)\n\nReturns:\nInteger value from FUN_1001fde6 if bit was set and no higher bits exist, 0 otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBitfield is exactly 96 bits (3 x 32-bit words)\nBit index 0x20 (32) targets second word, 0x40 (64) targets third word\nHigher bit clearing always clears from next word boundary to end\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x20 (32) - Bits per word, used for word boundary calculations\n0x1F (31) - Bit mask for position within word\n0x3 (3) - Total number of 32-bit words in 96-bit bitfield\n\nError Handling:\nNo bounds checking on bit index - caller must ensure 0 <= nBitIndex <= 95\nNo null pointer validation on pBitfield parameter\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwLowBits     | uint | Bits 0-31\n0x04   | 4    | dwMidBits     | uint | Bits 32-63  \n0x08   | 4    | dwHighBits    | uint | Bits 64-95",
