      "name": "AdjustFileBufferBounds",
      "signature": "int AdjustFileBufferBounds(int nHeapIndex, int * pBlockData, byte * pbBlockInfo, dword cbBlockCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Attempts to reserve and allocate heap blocks from a Low Fragmentation Heap (LFH) block entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load current block size from pbBlockInfo[0]\n  2. Calculate if expansion needed: if cbBlockCount < current size\n  3. If shrinking: update free space counter and mark block as free (0xF1)\n  4. If expanding: validate boundaries and zero-fill intermediate blocks\n  5. Scan for occupied blocks in expansion range\n  6. If valid expansion: update block allocator pointer and calculate padding\n  7. Return success (1) if allocated, failure (0) if validation fails\n\nParameters:\n  nHeapIndex      : Heap index/identifier for block allocation\n  pBlockData      : Pointer to block metadata (offsets 0x0, 0x4 contain allocator state)\n  pbBlockInfo     : Current block info byte (size in 16-byte blocks)\n  cbBlockCount    : Requested block count (in 16-byte units, 0x4e = 78 bytes ~= 5 blocks)\n\nReturns:\n  1 on successful block reservation or update\n  0 on allocation failure or invalid expansion attempt\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Block boundary: Validates against offset 0x3e (62 bytes, structure boundary)\n  Shrinking: Decreases allocated blocks, updates free pool\n  Expansion: Requires zero-filled intermediate space, may update allocator pointers\n  Boundaries: Data region limited to 0x40 (64) bytes total",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
