      "name": "Mul64x64",
      "signature": "longlong Mul64x64(dword dwLo1, int nHi1, dword dwLo2, int nHi2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "longlong",
      "comment": "64-bit multiplication helper: computes (dwHi1:dwLo1) * (dwHi2:dwLo2)\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. If both high parts are zero (dwHi1==0 && dwHi2==0), return simple 64-bit product\n  2. Otherwise, compute full 128-bit product and extract low 64 bits:\n     - Multiply: dwLo1*dwLo2 (64-bit result)\n     - Add cross products: (dwLo1*dwHi2) and (dwHi1*dwLo2)\n     - Result = (high 32 bits of dwLo1*dwLo2) + (cross products) << 32\n\nParameters:\n  dwLo1 - Low 32 bits of first multiplicand\n  dwHi1 - High 32 bits of first multiplicand\n  dwLo2 - Low 32 bits of second multiplicand\n  dwHi2 - High 32 bits of second multiplicand\n\nReturns:\n  int64 - Low 64 bits of 128-bit product (dwHi1:dwLo1) * (dwHi2:dwLo2)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:546c17e22a38a8e15c8829671ea3e893",
